# Phase 1 – Brainstorming & Ideation

## Project Title

**Streamlining IT Procurement: Automating Standard Laptop Orders with Flow Designer**

## 1. Introduction

The project focuses on improving the IT procurement process for standard laptop requests using ServiceNow Flow Designer.

The idea was developed around the need to reduce manual intervention when standard laptops require configuration after being requested.

## 2. Problem Identification

The existing process for handling standard laptop requests can involve manual work. Standard laptop requests require configuration, and this step can be delayed or overlooked.

This can result in:

- Delays in laptop configuration
- Increased manual work for the IT department
- Inefficient allocation of IT resources
- Increased waiting time for users

## 3. Proposed Idea

The proposed solution is to automate the laptop configuration task using ServiceNow Flow Designer.

The system should automatically create a Catalog Task after the relevant Service Catalog request is processed and approved.

The task should be assigned to the Hardware team for laptop configuration.

## 4. User Story

**As a member of the IT procurement team, I want a streamlined process for ordering standard laptops so that tasks are automatically generated and assigned to the Hardware team for configuration.**

This will help ensure that laptops are configured promptly and reduce manual intervention.

## 5. Initial Workflow Idea

The proposed workflow is:

Standard Laptop Request
        ↓
Service Catalog
        ↓
Request Approval
        ↓
Flow Designer
        ↓
Create Catalog Task
        ↓
Assign to Hardware
        ↓
Laptop Configuration

## 6. Expected Benefits

The proposed automation is intended to:

- Provide a smoother experience for users requesting standard laptops.
- Reduce manual intervention.
- Reduce potential errors.
- Improve task allocation.
- Improve efficiency in IT procurement.

## 7. Conclusion

The brainstorming phase identified the need to automate the standard laptop procurement and configuration process.

The proposed solution is to use ServiceNow Flow Designer to automatically generate and assign a configuration task to the Hardware team.
